Hi Pariksheet and Sean,

I've taken the first approach Sean mentioned: the plugin is published
through its own marketplace in the package's GitHub repository. Claude Code
doesn't read the plugin from the installed R package. It installs plugins
itself, from a GitHub repository added as a plugin marketplace, so the
files only need to be in the repository. They are listed in
`.Rbuildignore`, so they are not part of the built package and never reach
a user's R library. That also means nothing needs to be copied or linked
into a user's project.

Using the plugin is opt in. A section of the vignette will show the install
commands as code that is not run, for the user to enter in a Claude Code
session:

/plugin marketplace add genentech/basicBulk
/plugin install basicbulk at basicbulk

The GitHub repository is not public yet, so these commands won't work until
it is published.

I'm glad to hear this plan seems reasonable, and thank you for taking the
time to look at it.

Best,

Ben

